From c65b5d6833254872af107233abd29848122882da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: g00rek <76205606+g00rek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:07:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Homa Lawn: a stable device id, so a reinstalled phone is the
 same phone (patch 0038)

Reinstalling Homa Lawn or clearing its data makes a new link key, so the computer saw a new
phone and kept the old pairing as an offline duplicate. The phone now reports device_id:
lowercase hex SHA-256 of "homalawn-device:" + Settings.Secure.ANDROID_ID, which on Android 8+
is per signing key, user and device and survives a reinstall with the same key (a build signed
with another key is another device, which it is: it cannot update the other build). Only a
paired computer is told it: link.hello (paired), link.pair_wait (accepted) and launcher.ping.
Nothing is reported when Android gives no ANDROID_ID. The key is device_id because "device"
already carries Build.MODEL in hello and pair_wait.
